#{[17592186444759 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444759 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444759 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444759 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the constant term in the expression $7p+\\frac{1}{5}-3q+r?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444759 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2410df8a-af5f-5395-a8f7-6f01fb9b5a62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444759 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has four terms: $7p$, $\\frac{1}{5}$, $-3q$ and $r.$ The only term that does not contain any variables is $\\frac{1}{5}$, so $\\frac{1}{5}$ is the constant term." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444760 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444760 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171468" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444760 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444760 #edb/ref 1071 "The constant term in the expression $4m+7n$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444760 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2bd1aa13-179d-5d50-b799-cdeceb985d71" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444760 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has two terms: \n\n$$\n4m\\,,\\,7n\n$$\n\n \n\nEach of these terms contains a variable, so none are constant.\n\nThe constant term is missing. However, we can include it by adding zero to the expression. Rewriting the given expression as\n\n$$\n4m+7n+0,\n$$\n\nwe see that the constant term is $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444761 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444761 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444761 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444761 #edb/ref 1071 "The coefficient of $c$ in the expression  $\\frac{a}{4}-\\frac{2b}{3}-\\frac{3c}{5}$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444761 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3a1bccc4-dcaa-5037-affa-01c48877663d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444761 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: \n\n$$\n\\frac{a}{4}\\,,\\,-\\frac{2b}{3}\\,,\\,-\\frac{3c}{5}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe only term with the variable $c$ is $-\\frac{3c}{5},$ so $-\\frac{3}{5}$ is the coefficient of $c.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444762 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444762 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44235" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444762 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444762 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the coefficient of $r$ in the expression $\\frac{p}{3}+\\frac{2r}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444762 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b6ff78f-5ae9-5640-bff0-d028984b3a83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444762 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: \n\n$$\n\\frac{p}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{2r}{3}\\,,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThe only term with the variable $r$ is $\\frac{2r}{3},$ so $\\frac{2}{3}$ is the coefficient of $r.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444763 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444763 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44048" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444763 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444763 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the constant term in the expression $6-3x+2y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444763 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3f084ce4-122d-54f2-8959-73b35064d8ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444763 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: $6$, $-3x$ and $2y.$ The only term that does not contain any variables is $6$, so $6$ is the constant term." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444764 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444764 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175887" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444764 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444764 #edb/ref 1071 "The coefficient of $a$ in the expression $9a-2b+7$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444764 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3f37989f-b57a-5aea-8240-70da015f5138" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444764 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: \n\n$$\n9a\\,,\\,-2b\\,,\\,7\n$$\n\nThe only term with the variable $a$ is $9a,$ so $9$ is the coefficient of $a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175969" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1071 "The coefficients of $x$ and $y$ of the expression $x+4y$ are{{field-1}}\nand\n{{field-2}}\n, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50031aea-32a5-5fdf-84b7-ae97c029443e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444765 #edb/ref 1074 "The terms of the expression are $x$ and $4y.$ Looking at each term individually, we see that\n\n- the coefficient of the term $x$ is $1$, and\n\n- the coefficient of the term $4y$ is $4.$\n\nSo, the coefficients of $x$ and $y$ of the given expression are $1$ and $4,$ respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444766 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444766 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175371" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444766 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444766 #edb/ref 1071 "The constant term in the expression $3m-\\frac{5n}{6}+\\frac{1}{2}$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444766 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "62dea677-f3f9-594c-972b-a951f4087b85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444766 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: \n\n$$\n3m\\,,\\,-\\frac{5n}{6}\\,,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe only term that does not contain any variables is $\\frac{1}{2}$, so $\\frac{1}{2}$ is the constant term." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444767 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444767 #edb/ref 1069 "q-5003" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444767 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444767 #edb/ref 1071 "The coefficients of the expression $-2p-4q+9r$ are" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444767 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6fc23966-668e-556a-8201-5e4dfbc9499b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444767 #edb/ref 1074 "The terms of the expression are $-2p$, $-4q$ and $9r.$  Looking at each term individually, we see that\n\n- the coefficient of the term $-2p$ is $-2$,\n\n- the coefficient of the term $-4q$ is $-4$, and\n\n- the coefficient of the term $9r$ is $9.$\n\nSo, the coefficients of the expression are $-2$, $-4$ and $9.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444768 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444768 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101489" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444768 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444768 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the constant term in the expression $\\frac{1}{6}y-\\frac{4}{9}-w+\\frac{1}{5}x?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444768 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6ad512b-05d5-5a8e-92ba-aaa6e2d9bc0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444768 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has four terms: $\\frac{1}{6}y$, $-\\frac{4}{9}$, $-w$ and $\\frac{1}{5}x.$ The only term that does not contain any variables is $-\\frac{4}{9}$, so $-\\frac{4}{9}$ is the constant term." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444769 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444769 #edb/ref 1069 "q-176014" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444769 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444769 #edb/ref 1071 "The constant term in the expression $\\frac{3}{8}p-6-\\frac{3}{2}q$ is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444769 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8eb1f28-793c-5aac-9e95-717919e5f9cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444769 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: \n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{8}p\\,,\\,-6\\,,\\,-\\frac{3}{2}q\n$$\n\nThe only term that does not contain any variables is $-6$, so $-6$ is the constant term." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444770 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444744 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444770 #edb/ref 1069 "q-101493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444770 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444770 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the value of the constant term in the expression $7x-\\frac{2}{9}y-3z?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444770 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ebbf94e8-8bda-5e3a-9314-f9c7774a7046" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444770 #edb/ref 1074 "The expression has three terms: $7x,$ $-\\frac{2}{9}y,$ and $-3z.$ Each of these terms contains a variable, so none of them are constant terms.\n\nThe constant term is missing. However, we can include it by adding zero to the expression. Rewriting the given expression as\n\n$$\n7x-\\frac{2}{9}y-3z+0,\n$$\n\nwe see that the value of the constant term is $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
